ulams PHP runtime image - third-party software notice

This image is built from the official Docker "php" image (php:8.3-fpm-alpine) and installs
the packages below from the Alpine Linux repositories. They are unmodified distribution
packages. Their source code is available from the Alpine aports repository
(https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports) and from the upstream projects.

PHP and extensions (linked into the PHP process)
  PHP 8.3                         PHP-3.01
  apcu, redis (PECL)              PHP-3.01
  bundled extensions (gd, intl,   PHP-3.01 (libraries: see Alpine package metadata;
  zip, pdo_pgsql, ...)            libgd, ICU, libzip, libpq and others are permissive)

Tools copied into the image
  Composer 2.10                   MIT (https://getcomposer.org)

Command-line programs run as separate processes (GPL; not linked into ulams code)
  ffmpeg / ffprobe                GPL-2.0-or-later AND LGPL-2.1-or-later; Alpine builds it
                                  with --enable-gpl --enable-version3 (libx264, libx265),
                                  so the binaries are distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later
  x264, x265 libraries            GPL-2.0-or-later (used by ffmpeg)
  jpegoptim                       GPL-2.0-or-later
  pngquant, libimagequant         GPL-3.0-or-later
  gifsicle                        GPL-2.0-only
  bash                            GPL-3.0-or-later
  optipng                         Zlib
  supervisor                      BSD-style (Repoze; Alpine metadata: BSD-4-Clause AND BSD-3-Clause-Clear)
  unzip                           Info-ZIP licence

The ulams application calls the GPL programs through exec/process boundaries only
(php-ffmpeg, spatie/image-optimizer, supervisord), the "mere aggregation" case of the GPL.
Anyone redistributing this image must still offer the corresponding source of these
packages, which the Alpine aports repository and the package versions recorded in the
image (`apk info -v`) make possible.

Not included: install-php-extensions (MIT) is used during the build and removed afterwards.
